  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The ratio of yellow to white tulips in Mia's flower garden is $5:4.$\nIf Mia has $30$ yellow tulips, how many tulips are in the flower garden?",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $5:4$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of yellow tulips, and the denominator represents the number of white tulips.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 6}{4\\times 6}=\\frac{30}{24}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  Mia has $30$ yellow and $24$ white tulips. So, the total number of tulips is \n\n$$\n30+24=54.\n$$",
